# 1EG Passport — durable-URL redirect host (Cloudflare Pages `_redirects`)
# Project Blackbook HK09 Phase 2A / 2A.1.
#
# THE DURABLE PUBLIC CONTRACT IS THE HOSTNAME AND PATH, PERMANENTLY:
#     https://passport.greenglassvarano.com/1EG/<RecordID>
# The SharePoint destination below is REPLACEABLE IMPLEMENTATION DETAIL.
#
# ROUTING AUTHORITY IS SPLIT, DELIBERATELY:
#   /1EG/<one-segment>  ->  functions/1EG/[id].js   (the Pages Function)
#   everything else     ->  the rules in this file
#
# THE DYNAMIC RECORD-ID RULES WERE REMOVED FROM THIS FILE IN 2A.1. Cloudflare
# substitutes a captured placeholder VERBATIM AND UNENCODED, so a raw `&` in the
# path escaped the `p` parameter and created a second destination parameter —
# proven on the real edge. No rule below substitutes ANY captured value, so no
# rule below can be made to do that. Do not reintroduce a `:placeholder` rule
# that lands untrusted input in a query string.
#
# STATUS CODES — deliberate:
#   302 for the durable-host -> current-SharePoint hop. NEVER 301. The hostname is
#       permanent; the SharePoint URL is not, and a cacheable permanent redirect
#       would weaken future portability.
#   301 only to canonicalise an ALTERNATE HOSTING hostname onto the durable one.
#
# ORDER MATTERS — first match wins.

# --- everything under /1EG that is NOT a single segment : Passport Landing -----
# Covers /1EG/ (empty id) and nested paths such as /1EG/a/b/c — never fabricate an ID.
/1EG/*     https://dbgroupcorp.sharepoint.com/sites/1EG-PreservedItemCatalogue/SitePages/Passport.aspx  302
/1EG       https://dbgroupcorp.sharepoint.com/sites/1EG-PreservedItemCatalogue/SitePages/Passport.aspx  302

# --- bare host and every other namespace : Passport Landing --------------------
# Covers / and wrong namespaces such as /wrong/1EG-0001.
/*         https://dbgroupcorp.sharepoint.com/sites/1EG-PreservedItemCatalogue/SitePages/Passport.aspx  302

# --- CUTOVER-ONLY canonicalisation — DO NOT ENABLE DURING STAGING ---------------
# Enabling this while passport.greenglassvarano.com still points at GitHub Pages
# would make the Pages staging deployment untestable. Uncomment ONLY at cutover.
#
# https://<project>.pages.dev/*  https://passport.greenglassvarano.com/:splat  301
